    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 lineup today is headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 81.88. Facing the right-hander Severino, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+16%) and a favorable SP matchup (+15%), positioning him as the cornerstone of our attack. **Kyle Tucker** (69.90) and **Jacob Wilson** (69.51) follow closely behind as high-floor, high-ceiling plays; **Jacob Wilson** is particularly intriguing today given the 16% park factor uplift and his spot in the order, while **Kyle Tucker** remains a plug-and-play elite option against the right-handed Elder. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (67.25) rounds out our top-tier tier, leveraging a strong platoon advantage despite a minor BvP headwind, making him an essential piece of our 5x5 strategy.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was the exclusion of **Nasim Nunez** (53.72). While **Nasim Nunez** offers exactly the type of elite sprint speed we crave to address our scarcity in stolen bases, his projected ninth-place spot in the order (-8%) dragged his efficiency score below our threshold for starting consideration. He remains the first man up should a lineup change occur. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains on the IL; his absence necessitates a balanced approach across the outfield, where **Jackson Merrill** (66.44) is arguably our best leverage play today, given his excellent platoon setup and top-of-the-order role.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the volatility of our mid-tier hitters. We are exercising caution with **Sam Antonacci** (46.73) and **Heliot Ramos** (47.33) due to their matchups against high-skill arms like Gilbert and Chandler, respectively. While these players possess the talent to outperform their base projections, their scores are dampened by significant SP skill deficits. We are also keeping a close eye on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (57.41); while his xwOBA remains a strong indicator of future performance, the dynamic platoon disadvantage today necessitates a moderate expectation. All managers should be prepared to adjust if weather reports shift, particularly as we look to preserve our precious weekly game caps.",
